WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.912
Kublai Khan chose Dadu as the capital of the Yuan dynasty.

00:00:04.262 --> 00:00:10.742
Standing on high ground, he gazed over the wide plain, his heart full of hope.

00:00:11.092 --> 00:00:15.388
Craftsmen followed the plan and built magnificent palaces.

00:00:15.738 --> 00:00:20.346
Many craftsmen worked day and night, taking care with every brick and tile.

00:00:20.696 --> 00:00:25.784
The imperial palace gleamed in gold and splendor, magnificent in grandeur.

00:00:26.134 --> 00:00:31.702
The red walls and yellow tiles shone in the sunlight, visible from far away.

00:00:32.052 --> 00:00:36.348
Merchants from many countries came to Dadu, and the markets were bustling.

00:00:36.698 --> 00:00:42.218
Camel caravans brought spices, gems and fine cloth from far away.

00:00:42.568 --> 00:00:45.472
Dadu became the political center of the Yuan dynasty.

00:00:45.822 --> 00:00:50.646
The emperor handled state affairs here, and officials came to court every day.

00:00:50.996 --> 00:00:55.244
This prosperous capital is today's Beijing.

00:00:55.594 --> 00:01:00.850
Hundreds of years have passed, yet this story still lives in people's hearts.

